//! The Kotlin plugin's expression classes, `KExprProcessor.jmpWrapper` and the
//! `ResugarKotlinMethods` / `CollapseStringConcat` passes against Vineflower
//! 1.12.0 and its bundled Kotlin plugin (`data/kt5/GenKt5Oracle.java` over
//! `data/kt5/cases.txt` -> `data/kt5/golden.txt`, regenerated by
//! `data/kt5/gen.sh`, with `data/kt5/classes/kt5/KtProps` carrying the
//! property and infix-function attributes `KotlinChooser` would attach): text,
//! reformatted text, precedence, expression type,
//! type bounds, the expression ids each build and `copy()` consume, and the
//! classes `copy()` and the passes produce. The tree parser mirrors the Java
//! driver's, so construction order (and so every id) matches.
//!
//! Every row is compared; a row that reaches an `unported!` body fails.

